  "goodToKnow": "Der Satellit is a satellite: ein Wettersatellit, über Satellit empfangen. It's a weak noun: den Satelliten, des Satelliten. Many German households receive TV via Satellit, which is why you see Satellitenschüsseln (dishes) on balconies. Spelling trap: one t, two l's (Sa-tel-lit). Die Satellitenstadt is a satellite town, and East Germany was called a Satellitenstaat of the Soviet Union. From Latin satelles, bodyguard."
